{"name":"Dark Pansy","hex":"#653d7c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"pansy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cultivated flowering plant, derived by hybridization within species Viola tricolor.","A deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Wimpy; spineless; feeble.","Of a deep purple colour, like that of the pansy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pansy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Junonia stygia","blocks":[{"text":"Junonia stygia, the brown pansy, dark pansy or Aurivillius' brown pansy, is a butterfly in the family Nymphalidae. It is found in Senegal, Guinea-Bissau, Guinea, Sierra Leone, Liberia, Ivory Coast, Ghana, Togo, Nigeria, Cameroon, Gabon, the Republic of the Congo, the Central African Republic, Angola and the Democratic Republic of the Congo. The habitat consists of forests, including disturbed areas and secondary forests."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Brown_pansy_%28Junonia_stygia%29.jpg/330px-Brown_pansy_%28Junonia_stygia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Junonia_stygia"},{"title":"Pansy","blocks":[{"text":"The garden pansy is a type of polychromatic large-flowered hybrid plant cultivated as a garden flower. It is derived by hybridization from several species in the section Melanium of the genus Viola, particularly V. tricolor, a wildflower of Europe and western Asia known as heartsease. It is sometimes known as V. tricolor var. hortensis, but this scientific name is suspect. While V. tricolor var. hortensis Groenland & Rümpler is a synonym of Viola × wittrockiana, V. tricolor var. hortensis DC. refers to a horticultural variety of wild pansy that had been illustrated in Flora Danica in 1777 before the existence of Viola × wittrockiana."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b8/PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-PansyScan_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pansy"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Pansy_Flower.jpg/500px-Pansy_Flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pansy flower","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APansy_Flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg/500px-Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg/500px-Purple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pansy displaying the two upper overlapping petals, the two side petals, and the single bottom petal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APurple_and_black_viola_cultivar_in_Toronto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1